<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Interpreting Statements in Function Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00941</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Interpreting Statements in Function Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3964ba4f-76a0-4d37-99d3-9b335e002531</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Diego is walking home from school at a constant rate. This graph represents function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, which gives his distance from home, in kilometers, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> minutes since leaving the school.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Use the graph to find or estimate:</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        
          <media alt="Line graph showing kilometers from home versus minutes since leaving school. The line starts at about 2.25 km at 0 minutes and decreases steadily to 0 km at 20 minutes, indicating travel toward home.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">What is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, and what does it represent in the situation?
</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00007"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2.25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>; Zero minutes after Diego has left school, he is 2.25 kilometers from home, or Diego’s school is a little more than 2 kilometers from his house.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">What is <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0.9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> mean in the context of the problem, and what is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00015"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is approximately 10.5. After approximately 10.5 minutes, Diego is 1 kilometer from home.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00016">What does <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> mean in the context of the problem, and what is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 20. After 20 minutes, Diego is 0 kilometers from home, or it takes Diego 20 minutes to walk the 2.25 kilometers home from school.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>